@@ -9,6 +9,19 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Agent tools
+
+In browsers with [WebMCP](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api) enabled, the hydrated authentication forms expose these client-side tools:
+
+| Page | Tool | Required inputs |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `/devtools-times/signin` | `sign_in` | `username`, `password` (nonempty strings) |
+| `/devtools-times/signup` | `sign_up` | `username`, `password` (nonempty strings) |
+
+Tools submit to the same authentication endpoints as the forms and update their visible loading, success, and error states. Results are JSON strings containing `success` and either `message` or `error`; credentials and authentication tokens are not returned. Password policy remains enforced by the registration endpoint.
+
+Registration uses `document.modelContext`, with support for older `navigator.modelContext` browsers, and is cleaned up when the form unmounts during navigation. Browsers without WebMCP retain the ordinary forms.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
